<title>GERMANY: Buba says German Q2 GDP rose 1.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Buba says German Q2 GDP rose 1.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank gave the following details of Q2 1996 GDP data:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP   Q2 96   Q1 96	 Q4 95	 Q3 95</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    +1.5    -0.5(-0.4)  unch(-0.2)  +0.1(unch)</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+1.1    +0.4	  +1.1(+1.0)  +2.0</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)    765.6   754.4(754.2)758.0(757)  758.0(758.2)</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    +1.1    -0.2(-0.1)  unch(-0.2)  +0.1(unch)</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+1.0    +0.4	  +0.9(+0.8)  +1.7</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)    693.9   686.2(687.1)687.5(688.1)687.6(689.8)</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    +4.9    -3.4(-2.7)  +0.1(+0.7)  +0.6(+0.4)</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+2.4    -0.9(+0.1)  +2.3(+3.6)  +6.0(+5.9)</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)     71.7    68.2(67.1)  70.5(68.9)  70.4(68.4)</p>
<p>NOTE - The changes are calculated by Reuters from the Bundesbank GDP data. The figures are seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>Earlier the Federal Statistics Office gave the qtr/qtr figures but rounded to the nearest half pct point. Previously announced data in brackets.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
